sets/images/social/blog/2025/11/07/opentelemetry-signals-using-the-right-tool.png" type="image/png" length="58993" /> </item> <item> <title>What does &#39;good&#39; telemetry look like?</title> <category>Articles</category> <description>&lt;h1&gt;What does &#39;good&#39; telemetry look like?&lt;/h1&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://newrelic.com/blog/best-practices/what-does-good-telemetry-look-like&#34;&gt; &amp;lt;img src=&#34;/assets/img/good_...&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://www.dangb.me/blog/2025/08/08/what-does-good-telemetry-look-like/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 08 Aug 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://www.dangb.me/feed_rss_updated.xml">Dan Gomez Blanco</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.dangb.me/blog/2025/08/08/what-does-good-telemetry-look-like/</guid> <enclosure url="https://www.dangb.me/assets/images/social/blog/2025/08/08/what-does-good-telemetry-look-like.png" type="image/png" length="58993" /> </item> <item> <title>Platforms Are For Engineers, Not Services</title> <category>Articles</category> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Platforms Are For Engineers, Not Services&lt;/h1&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/assets/img/platforms_are_for_engineers/platform.png&#34; alt=&#34;Image of a train station&#34; style=&#34;float: left; width: 200px; margin-right: 12px&#34;/&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Ask ten engineers what a &#34;platform&#34; or &#34;platform engineering&#34; is, and you&#39;ll likely get ten different answers. Crucially, most of those answers will focus solely on the tech stack, not on how people interact with the platform. This trend needs to change. Otherwise, we risk disgruntled platform engineers frustrated by how their platforms are used, platform users who see technology adoption as a burden, and leaders who question the value of investing in an internal platform at all.&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://www.dangb.me/blog/2025/05/24/platforms-are-for-engineers/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 26 May 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <s